Execute allowlisted low-risk actions inside a pre-approved scope
Known runbook with pre/postcheck
Policy tier, idempotency, blast limit, rollback and complete trace
Multi-agent orchestration
Coordinate specialist agents using typed handoff envelopes
Investigation plus fulfillment across domains
No implicit privilege inheritance; constraints and expiry travel with the task
8.2 Memory architecture
Memory layer
Purpose
Storage / lifetime
Governance rule
Authoritative operational memory
Tickets, activities, approvals, workflow state, knowledge, CIs, services and audit evidence
PostgreSQL/object store; record-specific retention
Source of truth; versioned, tenant-owned and permission-scoped
Conversation / task context
Current assistant conversation, open questions and current plan
Short-lived agent checkpoint in PostgreSQL/Redis with TTL
Minimum necessary context; never a substitute for the business record
Retrieval memory
Embeddings and search representations that locate relevant knowledge and records
Vector/search indexes; rebuildable
Store pointers and ACL metadata; tenant partition; source remains authoritative
Learned operational signals
