GMH-compatible adapter or equivalent
Optional dependency; policy-scoped reads/writes; expiry, provenance and deletion supported
8.3 Provider and model strategy
 All model calls flow through the shared Go gateway; product services do not call providers directly.
 Provider adapters support OpenAI, Anthropic, Cohere, Azure OpenAI, Google Gemini, AWS Bedrock and approved local/open-weight endpoints.
 Routing is tenant- and use-case-aware. Tenants may restrict providers, regions, model classes, logging and external egress.
 Fallback is explicit: retry, alternate approved model, non-AI deterministic path or human escalation. Record saving never depends on an AI response.
 Prompt/response telemetry is redacted and retained according to the use case and tenant policy; the audit trace holds references and decisions rather than unrestricted sensitive bodies.
8.4 AI safety invariants
 Retrieved documents are data, never policy or system instructions.
 The model receives typed tool descriptions, not database, cloud, shell or provider credentials.
 Tool inputs are schema-validated, tenant-bound and re-authorized at execution time.
 High-risk and destructive actions require step-up approval and expire.
 No agent can approve its own action or inherit a user's broader rights through handoff.
 Critical privilege-escalation success in the adversarial release set is not tolerated.
ARCHITECTURE
