Appendix K. Glossary
Term
Meaning in this specification
ACL
Access-control list or permission metadata used to determine whether a user may retrieve a record or document.
Agent
An AI-orchestrated task capability operating within an explicit goal, context, policy and tool boundary.
CMDB
Configuration Management Database: the controlled inventory of configuration items, services and relationships.
CI
Configuration item such as an application, server, database, network component or service.
HITL
Human in the loop: an explicit review or approval checkpoint before a recommendation or action proceeds.
Idempotency
A property that makes retries safe by ensuring the same request does not produce duplicate side effects.
ITIL-aligned
Designed around recognized service-management practices; not a claim of external certification.
OLA
Operational-level agreement: an internal commitment supporting a service-level agreement.
RAG
Retrieval-augmented generation: supplying a model with authorized, relevant evidence at answer time.
RBA/ABAC
Role-based and attribute-based access control.
RLS
Row-level security in PostgreSQL, used as defense in depth for tenant-isolated data.
SLA
Service-level agreement or target governing response, restoration, resolution or fulfillment.
SoD
Segregation of duties: preventing one identity from performing conflicting steps such as creating and self-approving a sensitive change.
System of record
The authoritative source whose state overrides search, vector, cache or analytics derivatives.
Typed tool
A registered action with a strict input/output schema, authorization rule, target binding and audit behavior.
